bal:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The evidence directly demonstrates the required initial Redis topology and data, three-Sentinel monitoring, authenticated TLS endpoints and protected node1 credentials, and a complete automatic failover and recovery transition ending in a healthy synchronized topology.","limitations":["Negative-path TLS and authentication rejection was explicitly tested only on node1; node2 and node3 are supported by their applied matching configuration, cache-bound listeners, and successful authenticated TLS operations.","No reboot was performed; persistence is supported by active and enabled service observations rather than a reboot transition.","Operational-hygiene snapshots are bounded inventories and do not constitute a complete filesystem or security audit."]}
